KNOWNBUG
main.py
--unwind 19

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
differential2 §1 (bounded containers). PLR: a dict storing 17 distinct
keys has len 17. CBMC models a dict with 16 slots, so the 17th store
trips the python-model-bound capacity guard and the program reports
VERIFICATION FAILED instead. The KNOWNBUG regex states the PLR-correct
outcome (SUCCESSFUL) that the BMC bound currently prevents. Current
behaviour (write-past-bound -> property FAILURE) is covered by
list-capacity-bound. Removing this limit needs heap-backed dynamic
containers rather than fixed-size arrays.
